    "final_cot": "Image description: In the figure is triangle QPT, point R is on side QP, point S is on side QT, segment RS crosses the triangle and is in the same direction as base PT; RS and PT have the same arrow markings on them, indicating RS ∥ PT. The figure marks RS = 12, PT = 16, the entire right side QT = 20, segment QS is labeled x, and ST is required. Reasoning: Because RS ∥ PT, triangle QRS and triangle QPT are similar. The corresponding side ratio is RS/PT = 12/16 = 3/4, therefore QS/QT = 3/4. Given QT = 20, so QS = 20 × 3/4 = 15. Thus ST = QT - QS = 20 - 15 = 5.",
